          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शौर्यम् — śauryam — \"valour; heroism\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शौर्येण सः आहताय औषधम् आनयति। śauryeṇa saḥ āhatāya auṣadham ānayati. With great valour he brings medicine to the injured man."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "A neuter noun."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "शौर्यम् (śauryam) is usually traced to śūra, \"a hero\", with the lengthened first vowel; MW gives śaurya as heroism, valour, prowess (MW)."
            }
          ]
        },
